"""Korean-romanisation passages (hunter / regression / school register). Original prose."""

PASSAGES = [
("ko01", """The guild hall of [[Seongsu|l]] smelled of rust. [[Yoo Joonghyuk|p]] stood by the window, and the clerk, who liked old spellings, wrote [[Yu Jung-hyeok|p]] in the ledger. “[[Joonghyuk-ssi|p|tit]], the [[Hunters Association|o]] wants a word.” He did not turn. Another hunter called him [[the Regressor|t|ali]], and the trainees whispered [[Captain Yoo|p|tit]]. All three were one tired man. Rain hammered the glass. “Tell them I am busy,” he said, and picked up the dagger known as [[Black Fang|i]]."""),
("ko02", """[[Sung Jin-woo|p|si]] was not in the room, but everyone spoke of him. The new recruits said [[Sung Jinwoo|p]] with awe; the veterans said [[Jinwoo-nim|p|tit]] with irony. “[[Sung|p|wl]] is only a family name,” muttered the clerk. “[[Sung|p|wl]] what?” “[[Jin-woo|p]].” In the corner, [[Hunter Baek|p|tit]] sharpened a blade. Hope was thin that season. The [[Red Gate Raid|o]] would begin at dawn, led by the [[guild master|t]] of the [[Silver Crane Guild|o]]."""),
("ko03", """[[Kim Dokja-ssi|p|tit]] read on the subway as always. His coworkers knew him as [[Mr. Kim|p|tit]]; the readers of the old web novel knew him as [[Dokja|p]]. “[[Dokja-ssi|p|tit]],” called [[Han Sooyoung|p]], “you missed your stop.” “I know.” She sighed. [[Sooyoung|p]] had written half the story herself. At the next station the doors opened onto [[Jamsil|l]], and a crowd of strangers pushed in, none of them aware that the [[Star Stream|o]] was watching."""),
("ko04", """Two headmasters shared the island school. The [[headmaster|t|sh]] of [[Haneul Academy|o]] was strict. The [[headmaster|t|sh]] of [[Bada Academy|o]] was kind, and everyone preferred him. When [[Park Min-ho|p]] arrived with his transfer papers, [[Min-ho|p]] was handed to the strict one. “[[Park Minho|p]]?” the secretary asked, spelling it the other way. “Yes.” A bell rang over the harbour. In the hallway, [[Ji-woo|p]] stood waiting with a mop, pretending she had not heard a thing."""),
("ko05", """Nobody called her by her name. Rumours named her [[Lee Seo-yeon|p]], the guild's accountant, but the hunters said [[Seoyeon-nim|p|tit]], and the children said [[Aunt Lee|p|tit]]. Winter came early to [[Gangnam|l]]. “[[Seo-yeon|p]] unnie is late,” sighed [[Hana|p]], and set out the cups. On the shelf lay the contract for the [[Blue Dragon Dungeon|l]], stamped with the seal of the [[Cheongryong Company|o]]. The old [[chairman|t]] had signed it with a shaking hand."""),
("ko06", """Will it hold? [[Will Han|p|wl]] asked himself at the barrier. He was only half Korean, and everyone used his English name. His mother, [[Han Eun-ji|p]], called him [[Wooyoung|p]] at home. “[[Wooyoung-ah|p|tit]], eat.” At the academy his rival, [[Seo Hyun|p]], called him [[Han Will|p|ali]] to annoy him. The [[Black Turtle Society|o]] had sent a letter that morning. Nobody opened it. Snow settled on [[Mount Bukhan|l]]."""),
("ko07", """“Brother,” said [[Taeyang|p]], “the [[Tower|l]] opens tonight.” [[Tae-yang|p]] was nineteen and spoke too quickly. His elder, [[Cha Hyun-woo|p]], was known on the forums as [[Hyun|p]] and in the guild as [[the Wall|t|ali]]. “The [[Tower|l]] is not a game.” “[[Hyun-nim|p|tit]],” said the receptionist, “the Floor Ten gate is yours.” The old [[master|t]] of the [[Iron Lotus Guild|o]] was watching from the balcony, saying nothing."""),
("ko08", """[[Joy|p|si]] was the receptionist at [[Eunhaeng Tower|l]], and she was tired of the pun. “[[Joy|p|wl]] by name, not by nature,” she told [[Detective Oh|p|tit]]. [[Oh Sung-min|p]] only laughed. “[[Joy-ssi|p|tit]], I need the [[Silver Key|i]] logs.” She pulled up a dusty ledger. Neither noticed the [[president|t]] of the building company standing in the stairwell, listening. The elevator hummed. Somewhere below, the [[Third Bureau|o]] prepared a warrant."""),
("ko09", """[[Choi Ha-rin|p]] was eleven when the Gate opened over [[Incheon|l]]. Years later the papers wrote [[Ha-rin Choi|p]], the foreigners wrote [[Harin Choi|p]], and the soldiers called her [[the Little General|t|ali]]. “[[Harin-ssi|p|tit]], the [[Ministry|o]] on the phone.” “Tell them I am training.” The sword on her back was [[Daybreak|i]], a gift from her father. Hunters bowed as she passed the [[Hunters' Hall|o]]. She hated it."""),
("ko10", """“[[Professor Gong|p|tit]] is angry,” whispered [[Min-ji|p]]. “[[Gong Tae-sik|p]] is always angry,” said her friend [[Yun|p]]. In the lecture hall of [[Seorin University|o]], the [[dean|t]] was giving a speech about funding, and nobody listened. Hunter licences were on the agenda, but not in the way anyone wanted. “[[Tae-sik|p]] sunbae will fix it,” [[Yun|p]] added. Outside, cherry petals covered the steps of [[Dongseo Hall|l]]."""),
("ko11", """Her name was [[Rain|p|wl]], and the villagers of [[Cheongsan|l]] never let her forget the weather jokes. [[Rain Kang|p|wl]] kept her head down. “[[Rain-ah|p|tit]], the [[village chief|t]] wants you.” “Which one?” There were two villages sharing the valley and so two village chiefs, though in practice only [[Chief Bae|p|tit]] mattered. He held the old seal, the [[Jade Tiger Seal|i]], and he did not trust anyone under sixty."""),
("ko12", """The regressor's notebook listed names in two spellings: [[Yoon Se-ah|p]] / [[Yun Sea|p]], [[Baek Do-hyun|p]] / [[Paik Dohyun|p]]. He never knew which the system preferred. “[[Seah-ssi|p|tit]],” he began. “Call me [[Captain|t|ali]],” she said. “Everyone else does.” The two stood at the edge of [[Hangang Park|l]]. Behind them, the [[Moonlight Guild|o]] was burying its dead. “And [[Dohyun|p]]?” “Missing.” Nothing more was said, but the notebook stayed open."""),
("ko13", """[[Hunter|p|si]] was what the old woman called her grandson, after the sign on his jacket. [[Hunter|p|wl]] was no nickname; it was on his registration card. At the clinic of [[Saebyeok Hospital|l]] a nurse asked, “[[Hunter Jung|p|tit]]?” and the grandson sighed. His real name, [[Jung Han-gyeol|p]], appeared only in the grandmother's prayers. The [[Pale Sun Church|o]] sent flowers. “[[Hangyeol-ssi|p|tit]],” the doctor said, “the scan is clear.”"""),
("ko14", """In the north valley, [[Elder Moon|p|tit]] kept bees. In the south valley, another [[Elder Moon|p|tit]] kept goats. They had shared a name since birth but never a conversation. When the [[Council of Nine Peaks|o]] summoned the elders, both came, and sat three seats apart. “[[Moon Il-sun|p]],” said the speaker, and one stood. “Not you,” he added, and the other, [[Moon Il-seong|p]], rose in a huff. The honey cake on the table was called [[Sleeping Dragon|i]]."""),
("ko15", """[[Yeo Ji-an|p]] opened her shop at six. Customers called her [[Ms. Yeo|p|tit]], [[Jian-ssi|p|tit]], or just [[the Baker|t|ali]]. “One [[Milky Way Loaf|i]],” said a boy. “Please.” The bell above the door rang. In the street, a black car from the [[Haeseong Group|o]] idled; the [[vice-chairman|t]] was inside, watching her through tinted glass. [[Ji-an|p]] wiped the counter. “Plain bread,” she said quietly, “for plain people.” It was a lie, and she knew it."""),
]
